1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,045
Picture Chai Corner a few years from now.

2
00:00:03,045 --> 00:00:05,145
Five outlets, and fifty workers.

3
00:00:05,445 --> 00:00:08,574
But every worker still brings
every question to Ravi.

4
00:00:09,124 --> 00:00:10,303
Out of milk?

5
00:00:10,303 --> 00:00:11,242
Ask Ravi.

6
00:00:11,242 --> 00:00:12,947
The stove is broken?

7
00:00:12,947 --> 00:00:13,885
Ask Ravi.

8
00:00:14,185 --> 00:00:17,129
Ravi has no time left
to plan for the future.

9
00:00:17,429 --> 00:00:20,275
Fifty people, one manager,
and nothing moves.

10
00:00:20,925 --> 00:00:23,095
One manager cannot do it all.

11
00:00:23,095 --> 00:00:24,392
He needs levels.

12
00:00:25,092 --> 00:00:27,276
So, what are levels of management?

13
00:00:27,576 --> 00:00:31,714
They are the layers of managers in a
business, from the top to the bottom.

14
00:00:32,214 --> 00:00:35,228
Each layer has a different
amount of authority.

15
00:00:35,228 --> 00:00:38,036
Authority means the
power to make decisions.

16
00:00:38,686 --> 00:00:40,929
Most businesses have three levels.

17
00:00:40,929 --> 00:00:42,255
Picture a pyramid.

18
00:00:42,705 --> 00:00:44,716
At the top is top management.

19
00:00:44,716 --> 00:00:48,426
The board of directors, and
the CEO or managing director.

20
00:00:48,726 --> 00:00:51,925
They set the big goals and
the rules, called policies.

21
00:00:51,925 --> 00:00:54,677
And they plan for the
long term, years ahead.

22
00:00:55,227 --> 00:00:57,617
In the middle is middle management.

23
00:00:57,617 --> 00:01:00,048
Department heads and branch managers.

24
00:01:00,348 --> 00:01:03,616
They turn the big plan into
a plan for each department.

25
00:01:03,916 --> 00:01:06,241
And they link the top and the bottom.

26
00:01:06,241 --> 00:01:08,602
Orders go down, and problems come up.

27
00:01:09,151 --> 00:01:13,596
At the bottom is lower management,
also called first-line management.

28
00:01:13,596 --> 00:01:16,467
Supervisors and foremen, the team leaders.

29
00:01:16,767 --> 00:01:20,208
They plan the daily work, and
they guide the workers directly.

30
00:01:20,758 --> 00:01:21,929
Notice the shape.

31
00:01:21,929 --> 00:01:25,143
A few managers at the top,
and many at the bottom.

32
00:01:25,493 --> 00:01:28,327
The higher you go, the
further ahead you plan.

33
00:01:28,327 --> 00:01:30,194
Lower down, you handle today.

34
00:01:30,844 --> 00:01:32,494
Now, back to Chai Corner.

35
00:01:32,794 --> 00:01:34,400
Ravi is top management.

36
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:37,121
He decides where to open the next outlet.

37
00:01:37,421 --> 00:01:39,848
Each outlet manager is middle management.

38
00:01:39,848 --> 00:01:42,949
They plan the stock and
the staff for their outlet.

39
00:01:43,249 --> 00:01:45,927
And the shift supervisors
are lower management.

40
00:01:45,927 --> 00:01:47,567
They run the morning rush.

41
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:52,711
Now the broken stove goes to a
supervisor, and Ravi gets his time back.

42
00:01:53,361 --> 00:01:54,360
Quick check.

43
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:59,191
Who decides if Chai Corner opens ten
new outlets in the next five years?

44
00:02:01,091 --> 00:02:02,230
Top management!

45
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:05,108
Big, long-term plans are made at the top.

46
00:02:05,708 --> 00:02:06,717
So, remember.

47
00:02:07,017 --> 00:02:09,612
There are three levels:
top, middle, and lower.

48
00:02:09,962 --> 00:02:14,120
The top sets the goals, the middle
turns them into plans, and the lower

49
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:15,455
runs the daily work.

50
00:02:15,805 --> 00:02:18,610
And the higher you go, the
further ahead you plan.

51
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:23,738
Next time, we'll meet the roles every
manager plays, and the skills each

52
00:02:23,738 --> 00:02:24,698
level needs.
